    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.heaven",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Qian — Heaven",
      "description": "Trigram Heaven (☰ Qian, 乾). Three unbroken yang lines — pure yang, the Creative principle. Symbol of the sky, the father, the ruler, the dragon. Qualities: strength, initiative, perseverance, leadership, the indomitable creative will. In the Later Heaven (King Wen) arrangement, Heaven is placed in the northwest. In Chinese cosmology Heaven corresponds to the yang-metal phase. Western alchemical correspondence: Fire (or Air, traditions vary; Qian's pure yang energy is most often matched to Fire as the most active, ascending element). Qian appears as both upper and lower trigram in Hexagram 1 (The Creative), and as a component in many other hexagrams, lending its quality of strength and forward motion.",
