    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.earth",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Kun — Earth",
      "description": "Trigram Earth (☷ Kun, 坤). Three broken yin lines — pure yin, the Receptive principle. Symbol of the earth, the mother, the mare, yielding soil. Qualities: receptivity, devotion, nurturing, persistence, service, inexhaustible capacity. In the Later Heaven arrangement, Earth is placed in the southwest. Corresponds to the yin-earth phase. Western alchemical correspondence: Earth — the passive, receptive, form-giving element that receives the seed of Heaven and brings it to manifestation. Kun as both upper and lower trigram forms Hexagram 2 (The Receptive), the complement and equal of Heaven.",
