    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.thunder",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Zhen — Thunder",
      "description": "Trigram Thunder (☳ Zhen, 震). One unbroken yang line below two broken yin lines — yang energy erupting upward from below. Symbol of thunder, arousal, the firstborn son, the dragon emerging. Qualities: movement, arousal, shock, initiative, the sudden start, inspiring fear and reverence. In the Later Heaven arrangement, Thunder is placed in the east — the direction of the rising sun and new beginnings. In the five-phase system Zhen corresponds to wood (spring, growth). Western alchemical correspondence: Fire — the sudden spark, the activating shock, the explosive first movement. Thunder as both trigrams forms Hexagram 51 (The Arousing, Shock).",
