    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.water",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Kan — Water",
      "description": "Trigram Water (☵ Kan, 坎). One unbroken yang line between two broken yin lines — yang surrounded and enclosed by yin, like water filling a gorge. Symbol of the abyss, flowing water, danger, the moon, the middle son. Qualities: danger, flow, perseverance through difficulty, the hidden, depth, intelligence. Water always finds the lowest place and persists until it finds a way through every obstacle. In the Later Heaven arrangement, Water is placed in the north. Corresponds to the water phase. Western alchemical correspondence: Water — the flowing, penetrating, hidden element. Kan as both trigrams forms Hexagram 29 (The Abysmal, Repeated Danger).",
