    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.mountain",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Gen — Mountain",
      "description": "Trigram Mountain (☶ Gen, 艮). One unbroken yang line above two broken yin lines — yang resting on yin, the summit. Symbol of the mountain, stillness, the youngest son, the hand that stops. Qualities: stillness, stopping, resting, meditation, limits, boundaries, completion before a new beginning. The mountain keeps still; it does not force its way through but waits in perfect self-composure. In the Later Heaven arrangement, Mountain is placed in the northeast. Corresponds to the earth phase (transitional). Western alchemical correspondence: Earth — immovable solidity, the densest and most stable element, the foundation. Gen as both trigrams forms Hexagram 52 (Keeping Still, Mountain).",
