    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.wind",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Xun — Wind",
      "description": "Trigram Wind (☴ Xun, 巽). One broken yin line below two unbroken yang lines — yin penetrating upward beneath yang. Symbol of wind, wood (trees growing upward), the eldest daughter, gentle penetration. Qualities: penetration, gentleness, flexibility, persistence, adaptability, working slowly and without force to accomplish everything. Wind enters wherever there is a crack; the root of a tree splits rock in time. In the Later Heaven arrangement, Wind/Wood is placed in the southeast. Corresponds to the wood phase. Western alchemical correspondence: Air — the all-penetrating, invisible, moving element. Xun as both trigrams forms Hexagram 57 (The Gentle, Wind).",
