    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.fire",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Li — Fire",
      "description": "Trigram Fire (☲ Li, 離). One broken yin line between two unbroken yang lines — yin enclosed by yang, like the hollow inside a flame. Symbol of fire, the sun, the middle daughter, clinging brightness. Qualities: brightness, beauty, clarity, dependence (fire clings to what it burns), elegance, the eye. Fire illuminates everything around it but depends on fuel; it cannot sustain itself alone. In the Later Heaven arrangement, Fire is placed in the south. Corresponds to the fire phase. Western alchemical correspondence: Fire — the luminous, upward-rising, transforming element. Li as both trigrams forms Hexagram 30 (The Clinging, Fire).",
