    {
      "canonicalName": "iching.trigram.lake",
      "entityType": "iching.trigram",
      "primaryDisplayName": "Dui — Lake",
      "description": "Trigram Lake (☱ Dui, 兌). One broken yin line above two unbroken yang lines — yin floating on yang, an open surface over strength. Symbol of the lake, a marsh, a smiling mouth, the youngest daughter, joyfulness. Qualities: joy, pleasure, exchange, speech, persuasion, openness, delight in life. The lake is open at the surface and nourishes all that comes to it. Joy that arises from inner strength is inexhaustible; joy that depends only on external things runs dry. In the Later Heaven arrangement, Lake is placed in the west. Corresponds to the metal phase. Western alchemical correspondence: Water — the receiving, open, reflective surface; also associated with Air by some traditions (for the openness and communicative quality). Dui as both trigrams forms Hexagram 58 (The Joyous, Lake).",
